<title>DENMARK: Monberg &amp; Thorsen six-month profit mixed.</title>
<headline>Monberg &amp; Thorsen six-month profit mixed.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net result			 57   vs 60</p>
<p> Net result after minorities	  39   vs 22</p>
<p> Group net turnover		  3,678   vs 3,491</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Danish construction company is Monberg &amp; Thorsen Holding A/S, whole owner of Monberg &amp; Thorsen A/S, which has 24 percent state in MT Group, the international consortium building twin rail tunnels under Denmark's Great Belt waterway.  </p>
<p>The tunnel project is part of the fixed road-rail-tunnel-bridge link joining Zealand island, site of Copenhagen, with the European mainland via central Funen island, a project due for completion in the late 1990s. It said it expected similar net profits for full year 1996 as 1995's 193 million crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969650</p>
